// Single-action schema, aggregation flavor: a rate limit where the counted
// history predicate IS the decision action. "Permit a transfer only if this
// user has made fewer than 3 transfers in the last hour (including this
// one)." The count uses the 0179 shape (`formerly ... && tp(t)` inside the
// `where`) so it counts history, and `formerly` inclusivity means the
// current transfer counts toward its own limit.
//
// Trace: alice(@0), alice(@10), alice(@20), bob(@30), alice(@40).
// tp0: alice count 1  -> true
// tp1: alice count 2  -> true
// tp2: alice count 3  -> false
// tp3: bob   count 1  -> true  (user pin excludes alice's transfers)
// tp4: alice count 4  -> false

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). ((count for (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user } && tp(t)))) == n && n < 3)
};
